caymanslm: restore the Qualcomm IMEM download cookie (diagnostic, default n)

Groundwork for a TZ-SDI ramdump of the Duck Detector CPU wedge. Three separate
LG modifications make a Qualcomm ramdump unreachable on this device, and all
three have to be undone together before the SoC can even enter dump mode:

  1. msm_restart_probe() does `if (!download_mode) scm_disable_sdi();`. Our
     cmdline carries lge.crash_handler=off, so download_mode is 0 at probe and
     TZ's System Debug Image -- the thing that saves the CPU contexts at a
     watchdog bite -- is switched off. Writing the download_mode sysfs knob at
     runtime is far too late. Arm it before probe instead:
         msm_poweroff.download_mode=1
  2. set_dload_mode() has the IMEM cookie write compiled out under
     CONFIG_LGE_HANDLE_PANIC -- dload_mode_addr does not even exist -- leaving
     only the TZ SCM call.
  3. LG stripped BOTH qcom,msm-imem-download_mode and
     qcom,msm-imem-emergency_download_mode from sdm845.dtsi, so there is no
     address to stamp. Probe logs "unable to find DT imem DLOAD mode node".

This restores 2 and 3 behind CONFIG_CAYMANSLM_QC_DLOAD (default n). The two DT
nodes use Qualcomm's canonical offsets (0x0 and 0xfe0); both are unused by the
existing imem children (mem_dump_table@10, dload_type@1c, diag_dload@c8,
restart_reason@65c, boot_stats@6b0, kaslr_offset@6d0, pil@94c).

MEASURED RESULT: this is NOT sufficient. With the config on, both DT nodes
resolve (the probe errors disappear) and download_mode=1 at boot, so the cookie
is stamped and SDI stays armed -- and the Duck crash STILL does not enter
Qualcomm EDL. The LG SBL simply does not honour the Qualcomm download cookie:
it takes the crash reset itself, landing either in LG's own LAF downloader
(VID_1004/PID_6340) or in a normal boot. So the EDL / TZ-SDI ramdump route is
BLOCKED on this device by the bootloader, not merely expensive.

Kept because the diagnosis is worth preserving and the switch is default-n and
inert when off. Do not enable in a shipped kernel: any reset while dload is
armed would enter EDL.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
index 9044287e6fa5..1d52bd0594b2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
@@ -1938,6 +1938,26 @@
 			compatible = "qcom,msm-imem-diag-dload";
 			reg = <0xc8 200>;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * caymanslm diagnostic (CONFIG_CAYMANSLM_QC_DLOAD): LG stripped both
+		 * Qualcomm download-cookie nodes from this SoC dtsi, so
+		 * msm_restart_probe() logs "unable to find DT imem DLOAD/EDLOAD mode
+		 * node" and set_dload_mode() has no address to stamp.  Without the
+		 * cookie the SBL never enters Qualcomm dump mode on a crash, which is
+		 * why an armed download_mode still rebooted normally (or fell into
+		 * LG's LAF downloader).  These are Qualcomm's canonical offsets and
+		 * both are unused by the siblings above.
+		 */
+		download_mode@0 {
+			compatible = "qcom,msm-imem-download_mode";
+			reg = <0x0 0x8>;
+		};
+
+		emergency_download_mode@fe0 {
+			compatible = "qcom,msm-imem-emergency_download_mode";
+			reg = <0xfe0 0x20>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	qcom,venus@aae0000 {
diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig b/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig
index bfcd27e4e5ce..ce1d41929bc1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig
@@ -115,6 +115,22 @@ config POWER_RESET_QCOM
 	  Say Y here if you have a Qualcomm Tecnologies, Inc. board and wish to
 	  enable restart driver.
 
+config CAYMANSLM_QC_DLOAD
+	bool "caymanslm: stamp the Qualcomm IMEM download cookie (diagnostic)"
+	default n
+	depends on QCOM_DLOAD_MODE
+	help
+	  Diagnostic-only.  LG builds compile out the Qualcomm IMEM download
+	  cookie and strip its DT nodes, so a crash can never land the SoC in
+	  Qualcomm EDL dump mode -- the reset is taken by LG's LAF downloader or
+	  looks like an ordinary boot, and the TZ SDI CPU contexts stay
+	  unreachable.  This restores the cookie write (and the DT nodes come
+	  back with it) so that, with download_mode=1 armed before probe, a
+	  watchdog bite leaves the device in 9008 Sahara memory-debug mode for
+	  QPST QSaharaServer -m to collect.
+
+	  Any reset while dload is armed enters EDL.  Never ship this.
+
 config QCOM_DLOAD_MODE
 	bool "Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. download mode"
 	depends on POWER_RESET_QCOM
